note:
The shared machinery every input uses:
- the agent sees a change in any drop box and checks it (its shape, then the input's own checks);
- an error or a warning pauses taking it in, while the last good version stays in use, so a bad drop never breaks the map;
- a warning you agree with can be accepted (a button on the build page's banner, and a scenic command);
- the menu bar icon shows a warning symbol; the build page shows a banner per input with what's wrong;
- credits and licences come from the inputs' own description files into the catalog's credits.

Tried first on a test input; each input then moves onto it in its own task.
